course: dictionary
lesson: 15827
title: The underdog
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An underdog is the person or team that most people think will lose. Read the clues around the word. «Everyone thought the small village team would lose, so they were the underdog.» The words would lose tell you that the underdog is the one expected to fail.
explain: The word can also mean someone with less power or money than others. «Mia rooted for the underdog in the race.» Rooted for means cheered for, so Mia was cheering for the one who was expected to lose. Ask yourself: who was the weaker one here?
explain: Underdog stories are often exciting because the underdog wins. «The little robot was the underdog at the science fair, but it won first prize.» The surprise ending is what makes an underdog story special.
fact: An underdog is the person or team expected to lose a contest.
fact: An underdog can also be someone with less power or money than others.
fact: «Underdog» is a noun, so you can say an underdog or underdogs.
fact: People often root for the underdog, which means cheering for them.
fact: David and Goliath is a famous underdog story.
exercise: «The small team was the underdog before the big match.» What is an underdog here? | *The team expected to lose | The team with the most fans | The referee | The team that always wins
exercise: Which phrase means cheering for the weaker side? | *Root for the underdog | Ignore the underdog | Stop the underdog | Forget the underdog
exercise: «Everyone cheered when the underdog scored the winning goal.» Find and copy one word that is the noun for someone expected to lose. | winning | *underdog | cheered | goal
test: «Nobody thought the young runner could win, but she was the underdog who crossed the line first.» Why is she called the underdog? | *Because she was expected to lose | Because she ran under a bridge | Because she was the oldest runner | Because she had the most medals
test: An underdog story is one where the weaker side does what? | *Surprises everyone by winning | Gets bigger and stronger than the others | Stops the game | Always loses
exam: Which sentence uses underdog correctly to mean someone with less power or money? | The underdog was a sunny day at the beach | Everyone wanted the rich boy to win, but the poor girl was the underdog in the fight for fairness | *Everyone said the poor girl had no chance, so she was the underdog | The underdog was the winner of the cup every year
